<title>JAPAN: Daiki, Toyota units to make aluminium alloy in U.S.</title>
<headline>Daiki, Toyota units to make aluminium alloy in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daiki Aluminium Industry Co Ltd said on Thursday one of its units and a Toyota Tsusho Corp unit had agreed to set up a joint venture in the United States to produce aluminium alloy.</p>
<p>Daiki Aluminium said in a statement that the venture, to be set up in July, would start producing 2,500 tonnes of aluminium alloy from late 1998 in the state of Missouri for sales in North America.</p>
<p>Toyota Tsusho America Inc will take a 50 percent stake in the venture, Daiki International Trading Corporation 45 percent and Toyota Tsusho five percent, the statement said.</p>
</text>
